At run time, N1-N7, N9 and N10 return 42 for '6*7' on both Node versions. N8 throws ReferenceError in Node, which has no self; it is a browser form, and the engine is bundled into apps/web. N11 shows that repl.start is reachable. N12, import.meta.resolve, passes too, but it only resolves a specifier and is not a vector.

Under --disallow-code-generation-from-strings, N1-N7 become EvalError, while N9 and N10 still return 42.

The guard is therefore still a spelling denylist. F-DG3-100 does not verify (see verifications.json). This is not a new finding: it is the same class, and the severity stays Low and non-mandatory because the shipped engine has no dynamic code (SEC-R2-16).

