FAIL, for one reason: F-DG3-100 (Low, non-mandatory) does not verify closed, so it stays OPEN.

The guard repair refuses five of the six round-1 forms in both guards. The sixth, globalThis['ev'+'al'], is still caught only by the scan. More important, both guards are still spelling denylists. Eleven one-token variants pass eslint AND the source scan: identifier or concatenated computed 'constructor' keys, getOwnPropertyDescriptor, computed destructuring, the AsyncFunction constructor, tagged templates, global/self indexing, process.getBuiltinModule('node:vm'), and node:inspector/node:repl imports. Nine of them return 42 for '6*7' on Node 22 and Node 24. This contradicts ADR-0024 §6 'Extended guard'.

The shipped engine is unchanged, has no dynamic code, lints clean and passes its fuzz tests and my probe C (65/65). The gap is a guard-coverage gap, not an exploitable path, and I raise no new finding.

Everything else passes on candidate 58ef3f47: typecheck, build, lint, openapi (270 operations), no-cdn, format, unit on Node 22 and Node 24 (1565/1565), integration twice (793/793, 27 migrations, contract 270 live, every p3-pending list empty), and validate --historical DG2 and DG1.

